        "externalName": "Melqart (Phoenician/Canaanite Tyrian deity equated with Heracles by Greek tradition from Hdt. 2.43-44; the Cadiz/Gades cult was the canonical Phoenician-Greek syncretic meeting-point; not registered as standalone entry per the registry's deity-only-as-required-parent-anchor principle)",
        "tradition": "Phoenician",
        "personId": "phoenician_melqart",
        "sources": [
          {
            "kind": "primary",
            "reference": "Hdt. 2.43-44 (Herodotus visits both the Tyrian Heracles temple and the Egyptian Heracles to investigate the equation; concludes the Phoenician Melqart cult is the older); Diod. 5.20; Sil. Italicus 3.21"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
